content.strength_and_weaknesses:
Strength:
- The writing is clear and easy to understand, with intuitive explanation on the basic ideas;

- Empirical improvements seem promising compared to baselines.

Weaknesses:
- The formulation in Section 4.1 seems quite trivial, which provides little new insight beyond EOT;

- As to AS-PGD, first-order acceleration methods have long been applied in adversarial attacks, e.g., [1] used SGD momentum and [2] used Adam;

- As to AFS-PGD, fixed random noises (as well as perturbation history) are also a common practice in previous work when attacking neural ODEs.

Refs:

[1] Boosting adversarial attacks with momentum. CVPR 2018

[2] Adversarial robustness through local linearization. NeurIPS 2019

content.clarity,_quality,_novelty_and_reproducib:
The writing clarity and quality are good, but the novelty is quite limited. I did not check the reproducibility (no code is provided).

Minors:
- The reference format used in this paper is all \citet, where in many places \citep should be used instead;

